## Map & Filter
Arrays have built-in higher order functions:

### .map() - transform every element
```ts
const nums = [1, 2, 3];
const doubled = nums.map((n) => n * 2);
// [2, 4, 6]
```

### .filter() - keep elements that pass a test
```ts
const nums = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
const big = nums.filter((n) => n > 3);
// [4, 5]
```

You can chain them:
```ts
const result = nums.filter((n) => n > 2).map((n) => n * 10);
// [30, 40, 50]
```


---
## Assignment:
MeTube has an array of video view counts. Use `.filter()` to keep only videos with over 1000 views, then `.map()` to format them as `"X views"`. Print each result.
